WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.422
The industrial DMZ is commonly described as Level 3.

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:05.475
5.

00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:12.424
It is a security extension to the traditional Purdue discussion, not an original numbered level.

00:00:12.424 --> 00:00:23.584
Its purpose is to create a controlled buffer between enterprise IT and site operations so ordinary enterprise systems do not communicate directly with control networks.

00:00:23.584 --> 00:00:27.585
Services in the industrial DMZ mediate necessary exchange.

00:00:27.585 --> 00:00:32.428
A jump host can provide a managed path for administration.

00:00:32.428 --> 00:00:37.272
A remote-access broker can enforce identity, approval, and session controls.

00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:42.536
Patch and antivirus repositories can stage content before it enters OT.

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:50.327
Data replication services can move historian information outward without allowing enterprise clients to query control systems directly.

00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:57.276
Monitoring, logging, authentication proxies, file-transfer services, and update gateways may also belong in this zone.

00:00:57.276 --> 00:01:03.804
The exact design depends on operations, but each service should have a narrow purpose.

00:01:03.804 --> 00:01:08.647
Connections should specify approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, and owner.

00:01:08.647 --> 00:01:13.912
Broad routing through the DMZ defeats the reason for having it.

00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:17.070
The DMZ is not automatically trusted.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:22.756
It faces connections from two environments and may contain high-value access services.

00:01:22.756 --> 00:01:32.231
Harden systems, separate administrative access, monitor traffic, patch deliberately, retain logs, and avoid using the zone as a general-purpose server network.

00:01:32.231 --> 00:01:38.759
Remote sessions should terminate or be proxied there rather than passing transparently into OT.

00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:46.551
A strong industrial DMZ reduces direct enterprise-to-control connectivity and creates inspection points for data and control flows.

00:01:46.551 --> 00:01:53.078
It cannot repair weak segmentation below Level 3 or poor identity governance above it.

00:01:53.078 --> 00:02:02.975
Think of it as one architectural layer in a broader defense that includes controlled pathways, least privilege, asset knowledge, and operational oversight.
